      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A 4.5‑mile coastal trail links Lowell Point to North Beach, with low‑tide sections revealing hidden tide pools and salt marshes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lowell_point_alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lowell Point sits on Resurrection Bay’s western shore, a thin strip of flat land between towering mountains and the water.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lowell_Point%2C_Alaska",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The gravel road that reaches Lowell Point snakes along this narrow strip, offering a rugged drive through mountains and bay views.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lowell_Point%2C_Alaska",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Although there’s no formal harbor, small boats can land on Lowell Point’s beaches, making it a quiet anchorage for local fishermen.",
